            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An injection device incorporating a dose delivery mechanism is presented where a spinning through prevention feature is employed to maintain dose accuracy. The spinning through prevention feature can take of the form of a brake to prevent a rotating driver from inducing rotation of a nut during dose delivery. Alternatively, the spinning through prevention feature can employ freewheel design along with nut and ratchet assembly that can move from a first to a second position.</p>
            </abstract>
